@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# Sendline
+
+Send USDC to anyone on Ethereum mainnet. Connect a wallet, type an ENS name or
+address, enter an amount, send.
+
+Stack: Next.js 15 (App Router) · wagmi v2 · viem · RainbowKit · TanStack Query ·
+Tailwind v4.
+
+## Run it
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # fill in the RPC url
+npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000/pay
+```
+
+`npm run build` · `npm run typecheck`
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Variable | Required | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC_URL` | in production | Dedicated mainnet RPC. Without it the app uses the chain's public endpoint, which is rate-limited and drops reads under real traffic. The `/pay` page warns about this in development. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` | for mobile wallets | WalletConnect Cloud id. Without it only injected wallets and Coinbase Wallet are offered — WalletConnect-backed wallets are hidden rather than shown as dead buttons. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` | for sharing | Canonical origin used to build absolute OG/Twitter image URLs. |
+
+## How it works
+
+**Chain.** Ethereum mainnet only (`src/lib/constants.ts`). A wallet on any other
+network gets a switch prompt instead of a send button.
+
+**Token.** USDC at `0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48`, 6 decimals. All
+math runs in base units via `parseUnits`/`formatUnits`; decimals are read from
+the contract with the constant as a fallback.
+
+**Recipients.** ENS names resolve onchain and the resolved address is shown
+before you sign — that address is what gets submitted. Pasted addresses reverse-
+resolve to a name when they have one. Rejections always explain themselves: no
+address set for the name, wrong length, failed EIP-55 checksum. Sending to the
+zero address or to the USDC contract is blocked; sending to a contract or to
+yourself warns but is allowed.
+
+**Prices.** ETH/USD and USDC/USD come from Chainlink feeds on the same RPC as
+everything else — no API key, no CORS. USDC is read rather than assumed to be
+$1. If a feed hasn't updated within its heartbeat the value is labelled `stale`;
+if it's unavailable the app says so instead of dropping the figure.
+
+**Gas.** The ETH balance sits beside the form and warns when it's low. Each
+transfer is gas-estimated and priced in ETH and dollars before you sign. A
+wallet with no ETH is blocked with an explanation.
+
+**Sending.** The transfer is simulated first, so a revert becomes readable text
+instead of a paid-for failure. One pending state covers the whole flow — click,
+signature, receipt, and the balance refetch — and is released in `finally`, so a
+rejection can't wedge the button. Wallet and revert errors are translated to
+plain language next to the action that failed (USDC's blocklist and pause paths
+included).
+
+**Theme.** Semantic tokens in `src/app/globals.css` drive light and dark from one
+place, following the OS. There's no in-app toggle to keep in sync.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+src/
+  app/          routes, metadata, favicon, OG image
+  components/   screen, form, fields, balances, chrome
+  hooks/        balances, prices, ENS resolution, fee estimate
+  lib/          chain + token constants, ABIs, amount parsing, error copy
+```
+
+## Note on `next.config.ts`
+
+RainbowKit imports wagmi's connector barrel, which reaches Base Account's x402
+payment code and WalletConnect's optional pino pretty-printer. Neither path is
+used here, so those optional peers resolve to nothing rather than being
+installed. Remove the aliases if you ever enable those features.
